# Trivy CVE exceptions — accepted risk only.
# FORMAT (one per line):  CVE-XXXX-YYYYY   # owner, reason, review-by YYYY-MM-DD
# Rules:
#   - Every entry REQUIRES a justification + review date.
#   - No entry may sit here past its review date without re-approval.
#   - Legacy (7.4/8.0) EOL CVEs are handled per-image in CI, not blanket-ignored.
#
# All review-by dates below are 2026-08-31 — aligned to policy expires_at
# (decoupled-seal model, PR #58). policies/vulnerability-exceptions.yaml is the
# machine-enforced source of truth for expiry; the review-by comments here must
# mirror its expires_at so the two files never disagree.

# NOTE: the former Caddy go-jose/v3 exception was RESOLVED and removed — the
# pinned caddy:2-alpine base (Caddy v2.11.4) already ships go-jose/v3 v3.0.5 (the
# fixed version), verified multi-arch. See docs/security/cve-2026-34986-review.md.
# (Intentionally no CVE id here: the validator greps this file for CVE tokens.)

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UNFIXED Debian distro CRITICALs (no fix available upstream). The enforcing gate
# runs --ignore-unfixed so these do not gate, but they are recorded here as
# EXPLICIT, reviewed exceptions per the vulnerability-management policy. Each is
# an essential package that cannot be removed; reachability is minimal. Re-review
# every weekly scan and drop the entry the moment Debian ships a fix.
# Affects: php-cli/fpm/worker/frankenphp (+ nginx perl-base, unfixed variants).
# owner: platform/security · review-by 2026-08-31

# zlib1g — CVE-2023-45853 (MiniZip integer overflow). Debian: will_not_fix
#   (Debian does not build/ship the affected MiniZip). zlib is essential.
CVE-2023-45853
# perl-base — CVE-2026-42496 (fix_deferred) + CVE-2026-8376 (affected). perl-base
#   is Priority: required (dpkg depends on it); not invoked by PHP/nginx runtime.
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-8376
# libsqlite3-0 — CVE-2025-7458 (affected, no fix). sqlite3/pdo_sqlite are bundled
#   in the official PHP image; apps use Postgres/Redis, not sqlite, in production.
CVE-2025-7458
# frankenphp base extras (no fix available):
#   libaom3 — CVE-2023-6879 (AV1 decoder); not used by the PHP app server path.
CVE-2023-6879
#   linux-libc-dev — CVE-2026-43185 (kernel headers; not executable code at runtime).
CVE-2026-43185

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Caddy Go-stdlib (gobinary) — the caddy:2-alpine binary is compiled against a Go
# toolchain whose crypto/x509 has fixable HIGH CVEs. "Fixable" only by an UPSTREAM
# caddy rebuild on a newer Go — we do not rebuild the caddy binary, and cannot
# patch the embedded stdlib in our layer. Accepted so caddy can ENFORCE the gate
# (state B); Dependabot watches the caddy digest — bump the base + drop these when
# upstream ships a Go-bumped caddy. owner: platform/security · review-by 2026-08-31
CVE-2026-27145
CVE-2026-42504

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# nginx krb5 — FIXABLE, owner-accepted, SHORT TTL. The nginx-unprivileged:1.27-
# bookworm base ships krb5 1.20.1-2+deb12u3; Debian fixed CVE-2026-40355 +
# CVE-2026-40356 in +deb12u5 but the upstream nginx base has NOT yet absorbed it
# (verified: pinned == current upstream digest). Kerberos/GSSAPI is not used by
# the nginx reverse-proxy/static runtime; these libs are transitive. Drop these
# + bump the base the moment upstream nginx ships +deb12u5.
# owner: platform/security · review-by 2026-08-31
CVE-2026-40355
CVE-2026-40356

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# frankenphp Go-stdlib (gobinary) — the dunglas/frankenphp binary is compiled
# against Go stdlib v1.26.4, which has a fixable HIGH (crypto/x509 class). Fixable
# only by an UPSTREAM frankenphp rebuild on Go >=1.26.5 — we do not rebuild the
# frankenphp binary and cannot patch the embedded stdlib in our layer. Same class
# as the caddy go-stdlib entries. Drop + bump the base when upstream ships a
# Go-bumped frankenphp. owner: platform/security · review-by 2026-08-31
CVE-2026-39822

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# caddy c-ares (alpine) — the caddy:2-alpine base ships c-ares 1.34.6-r0; Alpine
# fixed CVE-2026-33630 (UAF/double-free) in 1.34.8-r0 but the pinned caddy base
# has not absorbed it. caddy is a Go binary using Go's own DNS resolver; c-ares is
# a transitive base library not on the caddy runtime path. Drop + bump the base
# the moment upstream caddy:2-alpine ships c-ares 1.34.8-r0.
# owner: platform/security · review-by 2026-08-31
CVE-2026-33630

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# curl/libcurl4 (shared debian bookworm base) — Debian fixed CVE-2026-5773
# (libcurl SMB connection-reuse) in 7.88.1-10+deb12u15, but EVERY pinned base
# (php-*, frankenphp, nginx) still ships +deb12u14 (verified: no upstream base
# digest carries +deb12u15 yet). Runtime-RELEVANT (PHP curl ext links libcurl4) —
# short TTL accepted-risk pending the base absorbing +deb12u15; drop + bump then.
# owner: platform/security · review-by 2026-08-31
CVE-2026-5773

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# caddy curl/libcurl (alpine) — the caddy:2-alpine base ships curl 8.19.0-r0;
# Alpine fixed CVE-2026-6276 in 8.20.0-r0 but the pinned base (== current upstream
# digest) has not absorbed it. caddy is a Go binary using Go's HTTP stack; the
# alpine curl is a transitive base tool not on the caddy runtime path. Drop + bump
# the base when caddy:2-alpine ships curl 8.20.0-r0.
# owner: platform/security · review-by 2026-08-31
CVE-2026-6276

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# grpc-go xDS RBAC + HTTP/2 (no CVE assigned; trivy reports the GHSA id) —
# compiled into the upstream caddy (grpc 1.81.0) and frankenphp (1.81.1)
# binaries; fixed in grpc-go 1.82.1, upstream-rebuild-only. xDS unused; HTTP
# serving is net/http. Drop + bump bases when upstream rebuilds.
# owner: platform/security · review-by 2026-08-31 (aligned to policy expires_at)
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf
